# WHAT THE FINDING IS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `generic-api-key` fired twice on `apps/api/test/payouts.test.ts`, at lines
# 1151 and 1170 of commit `00cb1bbb`, session 476's payout-refusal case. Both
# values are TEST FIXTURE IDEMPOTENCY KEYS: hyphenated English words with an ADR
# number interleaved. The digit run is the whole of the defect, because it lifts
# a short readable label over the rule's entropy floor; the measured entropies
# were 3.640 and 3.682. No credential, no vendor, no wiring: `POST
# /accounts/:accountId/payout` refuses before it reaches a backend, and the
# values were typed by hand into a fixture. The literals are NOT reproduced in
# this file, in ADR-288 or in the session log, because a document quoting them
# would carry the finding into the record of the finding.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS IS NOT THE REPAIR FOUR EARLIER SESSIONS REFUSED
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS REPOSITORY HAS REFUSED A SUPPRESSION FOUR TIMES AND REWRITTEN HISTORY
# INSTEAD, and a session reaching for this file owes those refusals an answer.
# `docs/STATE.md:4219` and `:4286` both close on the same sentence: a
# `.gitleaksignore` fingerprint "buys green by keeping the thing that should not
# be there". `:3769` refuses a `.gitleaks.toml` allowlist because it "exempts
# the PATH permanently where the defect was one STRING once". `:7224` rewrites
# the commit rather than pinning it.
#
# ALL FOUR WERE ON UNMERGED BRANCHES AND EVERY ONE OF THEM SAYS SO. `:3769`,
# `:4219` and `:4286` each record a rebase plus `--force-with-lease` over the
# session's OWN commits, authorised by the founder before it was run, on a
# branch `main` did not yet carry. THE REFUSAL PRESUPPOSES THE REMOVAL IS
# AVAILABLE. `00cb1bbb` is an ancestor of `origin/main` (`git merge-base
# --is-ancestor` exits 0), so the only removal is a rewrite of the default
# branch, which invalidates every checkout and every open branch in the
# repository. ADR-288 and this row forbid it outright.
#
# AND THE SHAPE IS DIFFERENT IN A WAY THAT MATTERS INDEPENDENTLY. `:3769`'s two
# values were "a real provider's webhook-secret prefix plus sixteen hex
# characters: a credential BY SHAPE", and `:4219`'s was a real base64 image
# header bound to `const secret`. Those are things that should not be there
# whether or not a scanner notices. A lowercase hyphenated English label is not
# a credential by shape, by entropy or by origin, and no rewrite of history
# would be spent on it if the scanner were silent.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS SUPPRESSED, EXACTLY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO POINTS IN A HISTORY THAT CANNOT CHANGE. A `git` fingerprint is
# `commit:file:rule:startline` and every field is pinned, so neither entry can
# suppress the same rule in another file, at another line, or in any commit that
# does not already exist. THE RULE IS UNTOUCHED: `generic-api-key` still runs at
# full strength over every commit and every file, and ADR-288 section 5 records
# a seeded fake credential in this very test file being caught with these
# entries in place.
#
# NO `dir` ENTRY IS ADDED AND THAT IS THE POINT. The working tree was REPAIRED
# rather than suppressed: both fixtures were renamed forward to this file's own
# `idem-<word>` convention in the same commit, so `gitleaks dir .` finds nothing
# to ignore. A `dir` entry here would have been the weakening, because the tree
# is the half that could still be fixed. Only the immutable half is pinned.
#
# THE HONEST COST IS THE SAME ONE THE HEADER ABOVE NAMES: a secret committed at
# exactly one of these two (commit, file, line) points would be suppressed. A
# commit's content is fixed once written, so that is impossible rather than
# unlikely.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DEFECT THAT PUT THESE HERE WAS NOT A FIXTURE NAME
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `CI-05` FAILED ON ALL THREE OF #632, #633 AND #634 AND ALL THREE WERE MERGED.
# The merge ritual read six local checks and never opened the pull request's own
# CI. Had it looked once, `00cb1bbb` would have been on an unmerged branch, the
# rewrite would have been available, and this file would have gained nothing.
# ADR-288 section 7 is that finding. A THIRD ENTRY HERE IS EVIDENCE THAT THE
